   `quiet iack`, `gt write isr`): is it valid BY CONSTRUCTION -- does the named mutant change the named observable, and can the
   row read "green" on a build where the cell is wrong?  Is any new row vacuous?  Is `nonspec ip2` sound -- CP0 Cause bit 10
   read with Status.IE clear reflects the ISA bus's CPU line (cpu_mips.c sets `1 << (8 + 2)` on assert) -- and does inserting
   the two reads between the two polls change any OLD row's value (the packet says no: a command-port read has no side effect
   under either build, and `mfc0` touches no device)?  Is the relabelling of the both-columns device values to CONTRACT right?
