  42: ## 1. The repair, in one paragraph
  43: 
  44: v2e adds two sessions and six rows and relabels nine.  `maskeoi`: line 4 acknowledged (poll), THEN masked (OCW1 0x10), then
  45: the specific EOI 0x64 -- `maskeoi isr` wants ISR 0x00 in both columns (the fix's ISR branch; HEAD never sets ISR), and the
  46: F2b mutant `D_eoi_maskcond` (the ISR branch conditioned on the line being unmasked) leaves 0x10.  `speceoi`: both UARTs
  47: acknowledged (ISR 0x18, `spec isr both` 0x00/0x18), the specific EOI 0x63 -- `spec eoi one` wants 0x10 (FIX) / 0x00 (HEAD);
  48: `B_spec_isr0` (the arm clearing the whole ISR) reads 0x00.  In `nonspec`, between the two polls: `mfc0 s3,cause` --
  49: `nonspec ip2` wants Cause bit 10 = 1 in both columns (the acknowledge of line 3 recomputes with line 4 pending; `D_deassert`
  50: reads 0), and a command-port read WITHOUT another OCW3 -- `poll once2` wants the IRR 0x10 (FIX: the latch reverted after a
  51: SUCCESSFUL poll) / 0x83 (HEAD's unconsumed poll byte); `D_latch_cond` (revert only after an unsuccessful poll) reads 0x84.
  52: In `quiet`: a GT IACK read with nothing pending -- `quiet iack` wants last_int 0 in both columns; `D_gt_always` reads
  53: 0xffffffff.  In `gt`: a WRITE to the IACK register before the read -- `gt write isr` wants ISR 0x00 both; `D_gt_write` (the
  54: read-only guard dropped) reads 0x10.  The both-columns DEVICE values (poll bytes, IACK values) are CONTRACT rows from v2e
  55: on, not controls -- a mutant that reds one is a KILL, not an instrument failure.  101 rows in 14 sessions, 26 of
  56: them symptom rows.  The SHIPPED revision is v2f: v2e with `spec polls` relabelled a SYMPTOM row after v2e's own L0 leg showed
  57: its columns differ (HEAD 0x8383 -- its second poll re-reports line 3 -- vs FIX 0x8384); no other change, every measurement
  58: below is of v2f, and v2e's cycle artifacts stand as history.  NOT rowed, disclosed: the retire guard's two conjuncts (`D_retire_anypic`, `D_retire_anyline`: a wrong
  59: extra retirement is observable only with a pending count >= 2, which only host time produces -- filed `pit8253retireguard`
  60: with the band-row construction) and the two-SLAVE-request stall (`D_fold`: the owed `i8259cascline` row; `nonspec ip2` sees
  61: only the master-side recompute).
