1. SIBLING PARITY (each edited arm against its nearest sibling; an asymmetry is a row owed or a sentence owed)
   a. the specific-EOI arm (edited: ISR-only when in service, legacy consume otherwise) vs the non-specific arm
      (edited: lowest ISR bit).  Rows: `eoi acked`, `eoi acked3`, `eoi noack`, `masked eoi` (specific); `nonspec
      lowest`, `nonspec twice` (non-specific).  Asymmetry: the non-specific arm has NO legacy-consume branch (on HEAD
      its IRR effect was `irr &= ~isr` with isr always 0 -- a no-op), so an un-acknowledged 0x20 consumes nothing in
      either column.  SENTENCE OWED, recorded here: that is HEAD's behaviour kept, not a new refusal.
   b. the `case 0x0c` read arm (edited: acknowledges, one-shot) vs the `default` read arm (untouched, byte-identical:
      the raw scan).  Rows: `poll byte`, `poll isr`, `poll irr4`, `poll once`, `poll masked`, `quiet poll`.  The
      default arm has NO row: a read with current_command == 0 is OUTSIDE the contract (disclosed in the docstring).
   c. the two acknowledge sites: the poll read (pic1 rows `ack*`, pic2 rows `casc*`) vs the GT IACK read (`gt*`,
      `gtcasc*`).  Both rowed on both PICs.  Not rowed: a GT IACK read with NOTHING pending (returns last_int, as
      HEAD; OUTSIDE), a GT IACK WRITE (the read-only guard; no malta guest writes it; OUTSIDE), the MVME5500 path
      (pic1 == NULL; no witness machine; OUTSIDE).
   d. pic1 vs pic2: the poll, the EOI and the GT path are rowed on pic2 through the mc146818 line (`casc*`,
      `gtcasc*`); a MASKED poll on pic2 is not rowed (OUTSIDE; the mask logic is the same helper line).

2. CLAIM -> ROW (every added comment sentence asserting an observable consequence)
   "resets the highest-priority in-service bit (the lowest set ISR bit)"           -> `nonspec lowest`, `nonspec twice`
   "when the line is in service ... resets that ISR bit and leaves the request"   -> `eoi acked`, `eoi acked3`, `eoi acked isr`
   "when it is NOT ... the EOI still consumes the request as it always did"       -> `eoi noack`, `masked eoi`
   "the read after an OCW3 poll ... is the interrupt acknowledge"                  -> `poll isr`, `poll irr4`, `poll3 isr`
   "of the highest unmasked request -- the raw irr scan returned masked lines"     -> `poll masked`, `poll first`/`poll second`
   "One read per poll: later reads return the IRR"                                 -> `poll once`
   "Line 0 of pic1 is the 8253, whose pending-event count is retired here"         -> `rate storm` (band), `pit poll irr0`
   "a PCI interrupt-acknowledge READ is the acknowledge ... then in pic2"          -> `gt isr`, `gt irr4 after`, `gtcasc isr2`, `gtcasc isr8`
   "Nothing pending, no ISA PICs, or a write: last_int, as before"                 -> NO ROW (1c) -- sentence owed, recorded here
   "pic2's irq is the cascade line (bus_isa.c folds it into pic1 bit 2)"           -> `casc irr2`, `gtcasc irr2` (controls)

3. GUARD FIELD vs BODY FIELD (per predicate the fix depends on; the partition the body induces; who writes each)
   specific-EOI hybrid predicate `d->isr & bit` -- body reads `d->irr`, `d->ier`, `d->irq`.  isr bit written by: the
   helper (set), both EOI arms (clear), DEVINIT (memset).  irr bit written by: bus_isa assert/deassert/fold, the
   helper (clear), the legacy branch (clear).  The four (isr bit, irr bit) cells for line 4: (1,0) after an ack with no
   re-assert -> `poll irr4`/`eoi acked isr`; (1,1) ack + re-assert -> `eoi acked`; (0,1) -> `eoi noack`; (0,0) ->
   `quiet *`.  Line 3: (1,1) `eoi acked3`, (1,0) `poll3 isr`.  Line 0: (1,0) `pit poll irr0`.  ier bit {0,1}: `masked
   eoi` (ier 1, isr 0) and `poll masked`.  EXHAUSTED for lines 4 and 3 on the body-tested cells; SAMPLED on line 0.
   helper `pending = irr & ~ier` {0, >0}: `quiet poll` (0) and every ack row (>0); `d == pic1 && n == 0 && ptr != NULL
   && *ptr > 0`: (pic1, n 0, >0) -> `rate storm`, `pit poll irr0`; (pic1, n != 0) -> `poll isr` etc.; (pic2) ->
   `casc isr8`, `gtcasc isr8`; (ptr NULL) UNREACHABLE on malta (DEVINIT(8253) always publishes) -- disclosed.
   `current_command` {0x0a, 0x0b, 0x0c, other}: 0x0c rowed everywhere; 0x0a/0x0b rowed as the readbacks; `other`
   (the default arm) OUTSIDE -- disclosed.
