619-(line 2): `old_isa_assert` sampled with bit 2 CLEAR, `pic1->irr |= 0x04`, `isa_interrupt_common` re-folds bit 2 from pic2's
620-unmasked set (still 0x02), `new_isa_assert` = bit 2 != old -> the scan skips x == 2, finds x = 9 -> `last_int = 9`, ASSERT
621-the CPU line.  Nothing is stranded; the CPU line is low only between the two acknowledges inside one `lw`.
