624-**D5 -- THE RETIRE GUARD'S CONJUNCTS.**  GLM Q12: dropping `d == p->pic1` or `n == 0` from the retire guard is observable
625:only through a race, so no deterministic row exists; the main loop DISCLOSED both cells under clause (e).  The counter-
626:argument the floor invites: the guard DOMINATES the retire and its operands are body-tested partitions (pic1 vs pic2; line 0
627:vs other), so the cells are floor cells and a row is owed.  The main loop's derivation of why no deterministic row exists: a
628-wrong extra decrement is visible only if the count is >= 2 when the wrong acknowledge lands (count 1 -> 0 has the same
629-visible effect as the right acknowledge's own retirement), and the count reaches 2 only by two host-timer fires with no
630-acknowledge between them -- a wall-clock condition the probe cannot make deterministic (the carrier's host-timer rule).
