52-## 1. The defect and the fix, in one paragraph each
53-
54-**Defect.**  `dev_8259.c` had no interrupt acknowledge: the OCW3 poll read returned a mask-blind poll byte and set no
55-in-service (ISR) bit, the GT64120 IACK read (`dev_gt.c`, `GT_PCI0_INTR_ACK`) returned the last asserted line and
56-acknowledged nothing, and the specific EOI stood in for the acknowledge by clearing the REQUEST bit (IRR) of the EOI'd
57-line (on the chip an EOI resets an ISR bit; the request bit is cleared by the acknowledge).  Measured on malta: the EOI
58-drops a request a device still holds (`witness_20261025/`), and the 8253 timer -- its pending-event count never retired,
59-because the only decrement sat in a bus deassert the 8253 never issues -- was re-delivered once per 2^14-instruction
60-tick: **7,415 IRQ 0 deliveries in 180M guest instructions at a programmed 18 Hz** (`rate_explore_20261025/`).
61-
62:**Fix (design (G'), ruled at F2).**  A helper `pic8259_acknowledge()` moves the highest-priority UNMASKED request to
63-service (ISR bit set, IRR bit cleared, the 8253's event retired on pic1 line 0 through the machine's published pointer)
64-and recomputes the PIC's output line; the read after an OCW3 poll calls it and is ONE-SHOT (later reads return the IRR);
65-the GT IACK READ calls it (master, then the slave through the cascade) and returns the line; the specific EOI resets the
66-ISR bit when the line is in service and otherwise CONSUMES the request as before (the legacy path for machines whose
67-vector read acknowledges nothing -- PReP, footbridge); the non-specific EOI resets the lowest set ISR bit.  Edge-only
68-(both documented guests program ICW1 0x11); the `default` read arm is byte-identical to HEAD.
69-
70-## 2. SETTLED PREMISES (recorded resolutions, each with its warrant; the F2 record is `pass1_20261025/f2_20261025/F2_RULINGS.md`)
71-
72-2.1  `dev_8259.c` and `bus_isa.c` have ONE commit each (the upstream import); `dev_8253.c` was touched at the counter
73-     latch (#439/#440), never at the tick.  `CHANGELOG.md` has no `i8259eoiirr` hit before this round.  (git log)
74-2.2  The 8253's count has one writer (`++` in the host-timer callback) and no reset; `bus_isa.c`'s decrement is dead on
75-     every machine because `bus_isa_init` snapshots `isa_pic_data.pending_timer_interrupts` BEFORE `DEVINIT(8253)`
76-     publishes it (Astra, Grok; checked).  The fix reads the machine field at call time.
77-2.3  Both documented malta guests program ICW1 0x11 (edge) and EOI SPECIFICALLY (slave then master); NetBSD acquires the
