**Q3. What all of us missed.**

1. **The rate row's FIX side has no floor, and the word "deliveries" cannot be right as stated.** READ: section 1 ties HEAD's ~7,4xx to per-2^14-tick re-deliveries; section 4 says "FIX 0x03 = 3 deliveries in 180M instructions at a programmed 18 Hz". REASONED: 3 true deliveries is off by two-to-three orders under every mechanism the packet offers (18 Hz programmed, 65 Hz host base, batching, a session inside the ~3-minute leg); the only reading that reconciles all the numbers is that the row samples the 8253's *pending count* -- HEAD ~7.5k = never-retired backlog over a ~115 s session, FIX 3 = momentary residual -- which makes both "deliveries" sentences records defects and, worse, means **no row in the 84 measures the guest's actual timer-delivery cadence at all**: an edit that retires too eagerly (concretely: drop the `d == p->pic1` conjunct -- not among the sixteen mutants, READ, and the count is 0 in every non-pit session, REASONED) passes every row, every mutant, and silently drops malta timer events. NOT CHECKABLE which reading is true; the settling fact is one line of the probe (the rate row's read address) or the rate session's wall-clock duration, which the packet omits. This is my one insisted-upon change before landing.
